  "id": "Compound::DB00402 - Gene::2558",
  "verbalization": "Eszopiclone, a central nervous system depressant, is shown to interact with Gabra4 and Gabra2, both of which are involved in Gaba receptor activity. This suggests that Eszopiclone may influence Gaba receptor function through these targets. The evidence indicates that Gabra5, a subunit of the Gaba receptor, is a downstream participant in the Gaba receptor activity pathway, implying a potential role for Eszopiclone in modulating Gaba receptor function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Eszopiclone exerts its effects, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a strong, though not absolute, link between Eszopiclone and Gabra5, supported by the shared involvement of Gabra4 and Gabra2 in Gaba receptor activity.",
